Z||000000||Haze_Performance||09-03-2000||12:09 AM||||Will one fit the Auto Fiero?? <P>General Motors Performance Shift Kit, Three Speed Automatic <BR>Firmness, control and durability. This kit allows you to choose from crisp shifts to <B>full on race</B>. Warranty: 1-year limited warranty against defects in craftsmanship and/or materials.<P>Part#350 <BR>General Motors Performance Shift Kit, Three Speed, Holds 1st-2nd to any RPM. Backshifts at your command. Dual feed fixes 3rd burn up. 13 pan bolts. 1969-2000 Buick / Chevrolet / GMC / Oldsmobile / Pontiac , 3 Speed, Fits non-lockup type V6, 5.0L or 5.7L cars, trucks and vans.   $66.05 <P>OR<P>Part#350C <BR>General Motors Performance Shift Kit, Three Speed, Holds 1st-2nd to any RPM. Backshifts at your command. Dual feed fixes 3rd burnup. 13 Pan bolts. 1981-1991 Buick / Chevrolet / GMC / Oldsmobile / Pontiac , 3 Speed, Fits lockup type V6, 5.0L or 5.7L cars, trucks and vans.   $73.34 <P>Its at carparts.com<BR> <A HREF="http://www.carparts.com/parts/newsearch2.asp?OrderIdentifier=ID5962244802900022&reflink=38691-0-0-0-0&sourceid=2&parttypeid=3109&itemid=7228&autoidsearch=YES" TARGET=_blank>http://www.carparts.com/parts/newsearch2.asp?OrderIdentifier=ID5962244802900022&reflink=38691-0-0-0-0&sourceid=2&parttypeid=3109&itemid=7228&autoidsearch=YES</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Uaana||09-03-2000||12:12 AM||||Just a question, What's the diff between those and what the FieroStore sells?<BR>And are they worth the hassle?||||reg||3
Z||000002||theogre||09-03-2000||12:09 PM||||I'm guessing by those numbers and discriptions they are TransGo kits. Transgo does make kits for TH125 but I don't think those are them.<P><A HREF="http://www.txchange.com/" TARGET=_blank>Transmission Exchange Co.</A> has all the parts/kits for TH125. Also has TC delay units. Note: Some kits require tearing apart the tranny more than you can do with it in the car. Othere only need acess to the valve body. Trans Exchange can tell you what ever you need to know.<P>Fiero Store sells the TransGo kit acording to what I've been told.<P>ARe they worth it? Depends allot on the condition of the tranny to start with. They won't fix a tranny with problems. They are mostly intended to adjust the tranny to a frimer shift. They can fix certain things about a tranny to prevent problems or correct certain issues with shift timing. you have to look at specs for the specific kit.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-03-2000).]||||reg||1
